  "interpretation": "Colour-only Frobenius acts freely as two C3 orbits on the six coherent q=8 parent signatures. Retaining the equivariant colour object gives six singletons; taking its colour-orbit coequalizer gives the two frozen fibres of size three.  The frozen two-centre residual pairing commutes with the C3 generator and together they give a regular C6 = C3 x C2 action on the six parents.  This residual C2 is the frozen two-centre ambiguity; the calculation does not identify it with the ambient Gale deck involution.",
